 ### Robust Projection with Regularized Projection
 This variant specifies a noise schedule for Robust Projection that adds stronger noise at the beginning stage and gradually decreases it at the converge stage [S1, unofficial].
 - Optimization runs for 80 steps, which is empirically sufficient for a voxel shape to converge to the volumetric mesh [S1, unofficial].
-- Gaussian noise is added with a ratio $k$ in a linear scheduler to suppress distortion. Starting with initial ratio $k=0.1$, $k$ is decreased linearly to 0 over 80 steps [S1, unofficial].
+- Gaussian noise is added with a ratio $k$ in a linear scheduler to suppress distortion [S1, unofficial]. Starting with initial ratio $k=0.1$, $k$ is decreased by 0.5 every 10 steps until 80 steps are completed [S1, unofficial].
 
